[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4241313355","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118552#issuecomment-4241313355","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118552","id":4241313355,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc78zU5L","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-14T04:31:57Z","updated_at":"2026-04-14T04:31:57Z","body":"Note that the identifier is optional for lambdas. The approach \"if there's an identifier, use it; otherwise, use the entire function or its header\" is a bit inconsistent. It might be better to always use the function header (the part from `func` to `)`, or the return type if present).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4241313355/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4241337832","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118552#issuecomment-4241337832","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118552","id":4241337832,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc78za3o","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-14T04:40:11Z","updated_at":"2026-04-14T04:40:11Z","body":"I'm a fan of the idea to use the function header, but it looked like there wasn't a node whose range (start and end line + col) corresponded to that part in the parser. The closest thing I can think of right now is to use the start of the FunctionNode as the start of the range, and one character before the body's SuiteNode as the end of the range. But I wasn't sure how to determine what precisely that latter position would be, in terms of the column at least.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4241337832/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4241389598","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118552#issuecomment-4241389598","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118552","id":4241389598,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc78znge","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-14T04:57:30Z","updated_at":"2026-04-14T04:57:30Z","body":"We don't need a node for the function header, we need new overloads for `push_error()` and `push_warning()` that takes a source region as a parameter.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4241389598/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4244915689","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118552#issuecomment-4244915689","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118552","id":4244915689,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc79BEXp","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-14T14:58:35Z","updated_at":"2026-04-14T14:58:35Z","body":"It looks to me like at the point where `push_warning()` is called, we effectively only have access to the node tree, such as the FunctionNode for the whole function. Unless I'm missing something (which is very possible) I think the approaches could be:\r\n\r\n- Add code to the parser which stores the start and end positions of the function header for a FunctionNode, similarly to how all nodes store their start and end positions. Then we can simply get the header's range from those member variables just as we do with node ranges already.\r\n- Use the body's SuiteNode range start as the end of the function header's range. It might be tricky to get specific information about how to position the endpoint with lines and columns; I'd have to look more into possible ways to approach this.\r\n\r\nThese combined with the overloads that take raw regions instead of nodes could work, I think?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4244915689/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4285815262","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118552#issuecomment-4285815262","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118552","id":4285815262,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7_dFne","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-21T03:55:26Z","updated_at":"2026-04-21T03:55:26Z","body":"While working on my game project using 4.6.2, I just realized that `UNUSED_PARAMETER` performs the same highlighting as we were discussing `UNTYPED_DECLARATION` having here:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"2619\" height=\"277\" alt=\"CleanShot 2026-04-20 at 20 53 33@2x\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4c44a83b-49b4-4268-b6f5-d2ef3be47af2\" />\r\n\r\nI'll have to look into how that warning's range is determined, and see if the same can be applied here.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4285815262/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4290620795","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118552#issuecomment-4290620795","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118552","id":4290620795,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7_va17","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-21T17:42:27Z","updated_at":"2026-04-21T17:42:27Z","body":"So, I think the possible lead I posted about was a bust – it may have had to do with how Godot passes information about warnings to the external editors via the language server – _but_ in doing so, I dug more into the approaches we'd discussed, and now have it seemingly working well at highlighting the entire function header!\r\n\r\n<img width=\"458\" height=\"286\" alt=\"CleanShot 2026-04-21 at 10 36 31@2x\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8128f027-a3b3-44e2-9db0-87da9b85c977\" />\r\n\r\nYou can see here that both single-line and multi-line function headers have the correct range highlighted, as do anonymous lambda functions 🙂","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4290620795/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4386271359","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118552#issuecomment-4386271359","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118552","id":4386271359,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBXEwfw","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-06T08:24:20Z","updated_at":"2026-05-06T08:24:20Z","body":"Haven't looked at the code yet. But from testing this looks mostly great. I found one small bug:\r\n\r\nFor abstract functions the closing parenthesis is not included in the range (using LSP since its easier to visualize ranges in VSCode):\r\n\r\n<img width=\"327\" height=\"95\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4509a053-5972-4114-8b0d-72ac0b4fc564\" />\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4386271359/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4390321012","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118552#issuecomment-4390321012","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118552","id":4390321012,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBa77dA","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-06T17:05:40Z","updated_at":"2026-05-06T17:05:40Z","body":"Thanks for taking a look and testing it! 😄 \r\n\r\nI've pushed a fix for the closing parenthesis issue:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"476\" height=\"665\" alt=\"CleanShot 2026-05-06 at 10 04 23@2x\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e1fa4c13-4057-46ed-9f84-36658114e213\" />\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4390321012/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4408926907","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118552#issuecomment-4408926907","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118552","id":4408926907,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBsriuw","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-08T18:33:22Z","updated_at":"2026-05-08T18:33:22Z","body":"Thanks for the review and suggestions! I've implemented them in the PR.\r\n\r\nThe instances of `alloc_node<FunctionNode>()` that aren't covered by this PR seem to be for property getters and setters. I'm not sure if it's possible for getters or setters to trigger `UNTYPED_DECLARATION` on their own; from my little bit of testing, it seems that the property as a whole triggers it if its type is not defined:\r\n```gdscript\r\nvar some_prop:  # UNTYPED_DECLARATION triggered here, for whole property\r\n  set(value):\r\n    some_prop = value\r\n```\r\nAnd the following has an error:\r\n```gdscript\r\nvar some_prop: \r\n  #   vvvvv - Expected \")\" after parameter name.\r\n  set(value: Variant):\r\n    some_prop = value\r\n```\r\nSimilarly, it doesn't appear that GDScript will accept a return type for `get`, as it throws another error when trying to specify one:\r\n```gdscript\r\nvar some_prop: \r\n  set(value):\r\n    some_prop = value\r\n  #   v - Expected \":\" after \"get()\".\r\n  get() -> Variant:\r\n    return some_prop\r\n```\r\nUnless there are cases here I missed, it looks to me like there wouldn't be cases where the warning could be triggered here. That being said, since we have access to the parser and its tokens/nodes, I feel like I might as well at least give a shot at having it save the header range so that if someone wants to access this info in the future, they aren't in for an unpleasant surprise 😅","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4408926907/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4409030514","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118552#issuecomment-4409030514","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118552","id":4409030514,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBsx3cg","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-08T18:50:45Z","updated_at":"2026-05-08T18:50:45Z","body":"Header range has been implemented for property setters and getters!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4409030514/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4461536469","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118552#issuecomment-4461536469","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118552","id":4461536469,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABCe2k1Q","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos",